 :criterion-text
 "Bootstrap diagnostic criterion bootstrap/compiler-diagnostic-compatibility (Open): Every declared self-hosted compiler module emits the C15 structured diagnostic record and a diagnostic manifest naming its actual stable codes and source spans; seed diagnostic codes remain stable enough for conformance fixtures. Reject a missing or unstable seed code with BOOT2004 and a self-hosted diagnostic code gap with BOOT4006. Positive fixtures exercise actual seed and self-hosted diagnostic production against accepted code/span expectations, retaining the module/compiler/source identities, manifest and golden records. Negative fixtures exercise missing/unstable codes and lost or changed source spans. Produce the module diagnostic products consumed by the existing release stage-equivalence and TEST13 diagnostic-schema checks. Diagnostic drift without compatibility review fails BOOT3003; accepted deltas require the actual policy-linked GOV2 compatibility assessment and the release comparison report, rather than a producer-supplied success flag. Preserve C15 phase availability, generated origins, privacy/redaction and ordinary-development versus authoritative-migration distinctions; this criterion does not itself compare stage executables or admit migration.",
